  "summary": "code16/sharp: Server-side request forgery through an unanchored autocomplete endpoint check",
  "details": "### Impact\nAn authenticated attacker can call the Autocomplete API with the configured endpoint as a substring to request another server-side route.\n\n### Patches\nThe problem has been patched in 9.23.0 and pre-release version 10.0.0-beta.4. The regex verifying the endpoint has been anchored to forbid substring injection.\n\n### Workarounds\nUse `SharpFormAutocompleteRemoteField::setRemoteCallback()` instead of `SharpFormAutocompleteRemoteField::setRemoteEndpoint()`.",
